Customer Query Urgency Classification

Introduction:
This project aims to identify how urgent a customer's problem is by analyzing their queries. 
It helps the customer support team understand which problems need immediate attention and which can be handled later.
Based on the customer's query, the system classifies the urgency into three categories: High, Medium, and Low. 
This makes it easier for the company to manage customer requests and provide support at the right time.

Prompt:
Read the given customer query carefully and identify how urgent the problem is. Based on the customer's issue, 
classify it into High, Medium, or Low. If the problem needs immediate attention, give High. If it needs attention but is not very urgent, 
give Medium. If it is a normal question or a less important issue, give Low. Provide only the urgency level without any explanation or additional text.

